- Copper carries electrical signals; fiber carries light between electrical endpoints.
- Higher lane rates make copper loss and crosstalk harder to manage.
- Passive copper is attractive at short reach because it is simple and low-power.
- Optics extends reach and improves cable density, but adds conversion components, power and cost.
- Compare qualified reach, errors, power and serviceability—not just the headline bit rate.

Sources

- NVIDIA, ConnectX-7 Adapter Card User Manual, updated August 12, 2026: https://networking-docs.nvidia.com/connectx7hw
- NVIDIA, LinkX Cables and Transceivers: https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/networking/interconnect/
- NVIDIA, DGX H100/H200 User Guide: https://docs.nvidia.com/dgx/dgxh100-user-guide/introduction-to-dgxh100.html

